      "id": 1,
      "text": "George Forbush, a Pennsylvania farmer, planted the first roots of Ringgold around 1725, giving the community its early name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://localnews1.org/local-history-ringgold-a-small-community-with-a-lasting-impact/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "When the railroad arrived, Ringgold shifted from a farming village to a convenient layover spot for travelers crossing the Blue Ridge.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://localnews1.org/local-history-ringgold-a-small-community-with-a-lasting-impact/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Jacob Moats, a local inventor, built the first directional moldboard plow with cutting sheers in the area that would become Ringgold.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://localnews1.org/local-history-ringgold-a-small-community-with-a-lasting-impact/",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Peach and apple orchards flourished on Ringgold’s fertile soil, making the town one of Maryland’s most productive fruit producers in the early 1900s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://localnews1.org/local-history-ringgold-a-small-community-with-a-lasting-impact/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Two historic hotels, the Blue Mountain Hotel and the Buena Vista Hotel, opened in the early 1900s, drawing visitors to the nearby Pen Mar Park.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://localnews1.org/local-history-ringgold-a-small-community-with-a-lasting-impact/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Ringgold’s post office once served as a stop between Hagerstown and Gettysburg, linking the small community to regional trade routes.",
